course: dictionary
lesson: 15067
title: Words with a beat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things that happen in a steady, repeated pattern. Rhythmic is one of them. It describes something with a regular beat, like a drum going boom, boom, boom. «The rhythmic clapping filled the hall.» The claps came again and again at an even pace, so rhythmic means having a steady, repeated beat.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The dancers moved in rhythmic steps to the music.» The word music and the steady steps tell you the movement is regular, not random. Now try the check: swap in a simple word like regular and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The dancers moved in regular steps to the music» works, so rhythmic is close to regular.
explain: Rhythmic is an adjective, so it describes a noun. You can also say something is more rhythmic when it has a steadier beat. Watch the family of words: rhythm is the pattern of beats, and rhythmic is the describing word that goes with it.
fact: Rhythmic means having a regular, repeated pattern of sounds or movements, like a beat.
fact: Rhythmic is an adjective: a rhythmic clap, a rhythmic step. Its comparative is more rhythmic.
fact: In music, rhythm is the pattern of beats.
fact: In PE, rhythmic gymnastics uses ribbons and balls, moved in time with the music.
fact: In science, the heart beats rhythmically, in a steady pattern.
exercise: «The rhythmic clapping filled the hall.» What does rhythmic mean here? | Happy and excited | Very loud and sudden | Quiet and hidden | *Having a steady, repeated beat
exercise: Which PE activity uses ribbons and balls moved in time to music? | Sprinting | *Rhythmic gymnastics | Swimming | Netball
exercise: «The drummer kept a rhythmic beat all the way through the song.» Find and copy one word that describes the beat. | drummer | *rhythmic | song | kept
test: «The rhythmic tapping of the rain made Mia sleepy.» What does rhythmic mean? | Silent and still | Sudden and surprising | *Having a regular, repeated beat | Cold and icy
test: What is the comparative form of rhythmic, for a beat that is even steadier? | rhythmically | rhythmicest | rhythmicer | *more rhythmic
exam: Which of these is the best example of something rhythmic? | *A drum beat going boom, boom, boom | A cat asleep in the sun | A sudden loud crash | A letter arriving in the post
